From 5c5c45331129f61e28b8b912c6d7ad7e331e9be0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <jufangjian@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 02:25:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [rh2-integration] consume-time staleness as the single
 authority; drop events; no-progress limit; JIT drain after publish

DefaultDataBuffer.get() is the only staleness judgement: a negative lag
(oldest > current) or, for a group that claims formal admission, missing
version facts raises WeightVersionAccountingError (run-fatal via the worker
exception) instead of being filtered; --max-weight-staleness None still
means no filtering. Every drop (put-time aborted, dynamic filter, consume-
time stale) and every consumed group is recorded through one structured
rh2 event with task/group identity, drop_stage, reason_code, member facts
and the version numbers; drain_complete summarises run totals.
--rh2-max-time-without-accepted-group SEC stops the run when the trainer
has waited longer than SEC for a group that actually passes the staleness
judgement (drops do not reset the clock). In fully-async mode train_async
requests the next group after the publish of the previous step (JIT
drain), so booked staleness equals the lag at real consumption.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
